paragraphs.en:
The temporal rules implement deferred causation. The Fut ◊ {}_{\operatorname{\lozenge}} and Fut ○ {}_{\mathop{\Circle}
olimits} rules apply only when the sub-derivation has reduced the body to a single causable event; the effect is scheduled at b b resp. after n n time points. Since ν 
u only inserts a time-point when something is due, the intermediate time-points of a chain of ○ \mathop{\Circle}
olimits operators need not exist within a bounded interval; hence bounded intervals are only supported for a single ○ \mathop{\Circle}
olimits ( Fut ○ {}_{\mathop{\Circle}
olimits} ), whereas chains must be unbounded ( Fut ○ n {}_{\mathop{\Circle}
olimits^{n}} ). Deadlines are at least one time unit (resp. time-point) ahead, so that obligations created by ν 
u are discharged by a later call.

paragraphs.zh:
时间规则实现了延迟因果性。 Fut ◊ {}_{\operatorname{\lozenge}} 和 Fut ○ {}_{\mathop{\Circle}
olimits} 规则仅在子推导将主体简化为单个可引发事件时适用；其效果分别安排在 b 和 n 个时间点后执行。 由于 ν 
u 仅在需要时插入一个时间点，因此 ○ \mathop{\Circle}
olimits 算子链中的中间时间点不必存在于有界区间内；因此，仅支持单个 ○ \mathop{\Circle}
